### ==============================================================================
### DecisionHub Backend API Test Suite
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 1. HEALTH CHECKS & SYSTEM STATUS
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Root Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 1.2 Health Check (v1 API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health HTTP/1.1

### 1.3 Health Check (Legacy Path)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health HTTP/1.1



### ==============================================================================
### 2. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Register New User - Success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.2 Register User - Duplicate Email (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Duplicate",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.3 Register User - Validation Error (Invalid Email & Short Password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 2.4 Login User - Success (Captures JWT token for subsequent requests)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store the JWT token from login response
@authToken = {{loginUser.response.body.token}}

### 2.5 Login User - Incorrect Password (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 2.6 Login User - Unknown Email (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent.user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ==============================================================================
### 3. PROTECTED ENDPOINTS & AUTHORIZATION CHECKS
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Protected Endpoint Without Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Protected Endpoint With Invalid Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid-or-tampered-token-12345

### 3.3 Protected Endpoint With Valid Bearer Token (Passes Security Filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

